{"id": "EUVD-2026-81110", "enisaUuid": "f4edbb02-7337-3c5a-9f08-e042cb4b6703", "description": "A vulnerability in the sftunnel inter-device communication protocol of Cisco Secure FMC Software could allow an authenticated, remote attacker to obtain&nbsp;root privileges.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to unsecured deserialization of untrusted data over the sftunnel management connection. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending crafted sftunnel remote procedure calls (RPCs). A successful exploit could allow the attacker to gain root privileges on a device that is running Cisco Secure FMC Software and its high-availability peer.\r\nTo exploit this vulnerability, the attacker must have valid administrative credentials on a managed Cisco FTD device.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T20:08:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-18T03:55:58", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-fmc-mulivulns-4PsnFwvx"], "aliases": ["GHSA-355g-mjpr-92rq", "CVE-2026-20341"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0285bf63-d834-35f4-8270-abfb1c51b3f3", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.4.2.2"}, {"id": "06467f85-ab25-3855-9afe-9db4e60a26a2", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.2.5.1"}, {"id": "073eb1fb-4c9f-3827-b121-b887679ab0c5", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "7.0.1"}, {"id": "0b35994e-b5ad-3aab-9a52-07fc72df95b5", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Management Center (FMC)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "10.0.1"}, {"id": "0dba2a16-5c3d-3375-9e66-f04ba0bd2d71", "product": {"name": "Cisco Secure Firewall Mana